.env
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Build artefacts. The results JSON and the leaderboard are results and stay committed.
output/run.log
output/selftest-*.pdf
output/overlays/selftest.png

# Per-case records are regenerable and mostly duplicate results-<model>.json.
# One is kept: the worked example the README walks through, so a reader can
# read a full probe trail - raw model text and all - without running anything.
# `output/cases/*`, not `output/cases/` - git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded, so the negation below would never fire.
output/cases/*
!output/cases/CXR-0050.json

# The open-i text index is 6 MB of derived data, rebuildable with `build`.
data/reference/openi_index.json

# Case folders hold resized IU-Xray frontals. open-i is CC BY-ND: a resized
# copy is a derivative and redistributing it is not ours to do. The committed
# probe file names every study by uid, so `build` re-fetches exactly these
# images from the Hub. The same goes for the downloaded demo films and the
# generated lab PDFs, which `build` mints deterministically.
data/cases/

# Downloaded demo assets - public, but not ours to redistribute.
data/demo/

# Paid deliverables - keep local
build-*-guide.md
*-instagram-assets.md
